# Group Files in Folders

Keep source directories organized by **feature/domain group folders** rather than
a flat pile of files. When adding a new file, place it in the folder for its group;
create the folder if it does not exist yet.

## Rules

- Every file must live inside a group folder that reflects its concern
  (e.g. `auth/`, `chat/`, `layout/`, `interrupts/`, `dashboard/`, `tool-display/`).
- Never leave loose files directly under a broad directory like `components/`,
  `lib/`, or `hooks/` when a logical group exists or can be created.
- When a group grows a distinct sub-concern, nest a subfolder
  (e.g. `chat/messages/` for message renderers).
- When moving existing files, use `git mv` to preserve history and update all
  `@/...` import paths.

## Example

```
// ❌ BAD — flat, ungrouped
components/
  login-page.tsx
  chat-sidebar.tsx
  thread-history.tsx
  app-layout.tsx

// ✅ GOOD — grouped by concern
components/
  auth/
    login-page.tsx
  chat/
    chat-sidebar.tsx
    thread-history.tsx
  layout/
    app-layout.tsx
```
